# Web building blocks (積木規則) — Tier 2 架構憲法

**Rule hierarchy:** **Tier 1** = security constitution (`security.md`). **This file = Tier 2** — applies to every new write in `apps/web`, directly below Tier 1.

**Victor standing order (2026-08-27, elevated 2026-08-30):** Do **not** wait for him to say「照積木規則」.  
Every new `apps/web` feature, component, button, chrome, or logic must land in the right block **on the first write**.  
The codebase is still being organized — skipping Tier 2 now makes later cleanup **much harder**.

Forbidden: paste into `app.js` / `c/app.js` / surface `styles.css` “to show quickly”, then refactor into `shell/` or `domains/` after he complains. Forbidden: 「稍後再拆積木」 / 「先寫在 app.js 再搬」.

Reference: adopted `20260813-web-layered-building-blocks` + `apps/web/domains/*` + `apps/web/shell/*`.

## When this applies

- Any **new** product logic, UI chrome, nav, dock, menu, sync paint, or shared styles for `apps/web` (C and covers onto B)
- Self-iteration Builder / in-chat “先做一個…” drafts on C — **same rule**
- Exempt only: typos, comment-only, or a one-line copy tweak Victor scoped in chat

## Hard stop — write order

```text
1. Classify layer (domain | core | shell | runtime)
2. Create/extend file under that folder
3. Thin-wire from surface app.js + index.html script/link tags
4. Only then paint DOM / go() / i18n in the facade
```

If you cannot name the target path (`apps/web/shell/<x>.js` or `apps/web/domains/<x>/…`) **before** typing implementation, stop and classify first.

**Never:**

- Grow algorithms inside `apps/web/app.js` or `apps/web/c/app.js`
- Duplicate the same chrome HTML/CSS in both C and B surfaces
- Put shared floating-chrome CSS only in `c/styles.css` / `styles.css` (use `shell/<name>.css` when C and B share it)

## Default workflow (must follow)

1. **Classify** — Which layer owns this brain? (table below)
2. **Write the block** — `domains/` / `core/` / `shell/` (IIFE + `PetLiveWeb.domains.*` or `PetLiveWeb.shell.*`)
3. **Wire** — Thin facade: `initX` / `paintX` that call the public API; pass hooks (`getActiveScreen`, `onGo`, `t` via re-apply i18n)
4. **Load** — `<script defer src="…">` and/or `<link rel="stylesheet" href="…">` in surface `index.html` **before** `app.js` (bump `?v=`)
5. **Test** — Prefer `qa/tests/web-<domain>.test.js` or `web-shell-*.test.js` (node:test + vm)

## Layers (put code here)

| Layer | Path | Owns | Must not |
|-------|------|------|----------|
| Domain | `apps/web/domains/<name>/` | Pure selectors / controllers / adapters on `pets[]` | DOM, `localStorage`, `t()`, another domain’s private state |
| Core | `apps/web/core/` | Shared state, storage slots | Screen HTML |
| Shell | `apps/web/shell/` | Navigation, **floating chrome**, docks, account menus, render coordinator | Pet/domain writes, direct storage |
| Runtime | `apps/web/runtime/` | `PetLive.*` bridges / ModuleResult unwrap | UI chrome |
| Surface facade | `apps/web/c/app.js` or `apps/web/app.js` | Compose factories, DOM events, i18n apply | Duplicate domain / chrome algorithms or markup |

Existing domains (reuse before inventing): `pets`, `visits`, `timeline`, `medications`, `alerts`, `vaccines`, `parasite`, `emergency`, `cloud`, `owner`, `breed`, `labs`, `imaging`.

Existing shell chrome (extend — do not re-paste into `app.js`):  
`navigation.js`, `app-nav.js`, `account-chrome.js`, `intro-cloud.js`, `glass-dock.js` (+ `glass-dock.css`), …

## Quick classify

| What Victor asked for | Put it here |
|---|---|
| Floating top/bottom glass bar, tab dock, account chip/popover | `shell/<name>.js` (+ shared `shell/<name>.css`) |
| Screen map / `go()` chrome paint / tab→screen key | `shell/` pure helpers + paint |
| Pet visits, meds, vaccines, alerts, labs, imaging logic | `domains/<name>/` |
| Storage keys / slots / sync-meta math without DOM | `core/` or domain selectors |
| One surface’s `data-go` / `hideOnScreens` / `passportGo` only | Thin facade args into shell `init*` |

**Rule of thumb:** If it is not writing `pets[]` / domain records, and it is nav or floating chrome → **shell**, not domain, not `app.js`.

## Chrome / nav UI (hard rule)

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| New/extend `apps/web/shell/<name>.js` | Paste `paint*` / tab-map into `app.js` or `c/app.js` |
| Shared chrome CSS in `apps/web/shell/<name>.css` | Copy dock CSS into both `styles.css` files |
| Markup factory on shell, mounted by `init*` | Duplicate large `<nav>` blocks in both `index.html`s |
| Facade: thin `initX` / `paintX` + hooks | Grow `go()` with chrome algorithms |

## Dependency direction

```text
index / bootstrap → shell → domain controllers → core state/storage → runtime → modules/*
views/facades → selectors + i18n
controllers -X-> DOM
views       -X-> localStorage
domains     -X-> another domain’s private internals
```

## Planner / Builder / in-chat agent must

- **Before coding:** state the target path in one line (e.g. `shell/glass-dock.js` + `shell/glass-dock.css`).
- **Planner proposals:** name layer + path + facade + script/link tags. Non-goal: dumping brain into `app.js`.
- **Builder / direct edits:** implement block files **first**; facade last.
- **C first** for passport shell per `c-to-b-cover`; shared `domains/*` and `shell/*` serve both surfaces.

## Done check (before telling Victor it’s done)

- [ ] Named the layer/path **before** implementing
- [ ] New brain lives under `domains/` / `core/` / `shell/` (not only `app.js`)
- [ ] Shared chrome CSS/markup not duplicated across C and B
- [ ] Surface `app.js` only wires + renders
- [ ] `index.html` loads the block (`?v=` bumped) before `app.js`
- [ ] No “稍後再拆” debt left for Victor to catch
- [ ] No second pet store; `pets[]` remains write truth unless a proposal explicitly changes that
